-- ccc12-part9-robbery-extortion.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Robbery and Extortion": sections 343 to 346.1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision; never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The offences named by section number in subsections 344(2) and 346(1.2) are tested against the core record `Provision of the Code` (PLAN.md seam rule R1).

§ `Robbery and Extortion (ss 343 to 346.1)`

§§ `Section 343 -- robbery`

-- src:6750 | Robbery
-- src:6751 | 343 Every one commits robbery who
-- src:6752 | (a) steals, and for the purpose of extorting whatever is stolen or to prevent or overcome resistance to the stealing, uses violence or threats of violence to a person or property;
-- src:6753 | (b) steals from any person and, at the time he steals or immediately before or immediately thereafter, wounds, beats, strikes or uses any personal violence to that person;
-- src:6754 | (c) assaults any person with intent to steal from him; or
-- src:6755 | (d) steals from any person while armed with an offensive weapon or imitation thereof.
@ref Criminal Code s 343 (src:6750-6755)
GIVEN `the person steals, by s 2 steal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person, for the purpose of extorting whatever is stolen or to prevent or overcome resistance to the stealing, uses violence or threats of violence to a person or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person steals from any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the person steals or immediately before or immediately thereafter, the person wounds, beats, strikes or uses any personal violence to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person assaults any person with intent to steal from them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is armed with an offensive weapon, by s 2 offensive weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is armed with an imitation of an offensive weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343 the person commits robbery` MEANS
    `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `para (a)` `para (b)`) (`ccc12 or` `para (c)` `para (d)`)
    -- JUST FALSE where no paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits robbery who"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 2 "steal" or s 2 "offensive weapon" answer was not given and no paragraph is otherwise settled
    WHERE
        `para (a)` MEANS `ccc12 and` `the person steals, by s 2 steal` (JUST `the person, for the purpose of extorting whatever is stolen or to prevent or overcome resistance to the stealing, uses violence or threats of violence to a person or property`)
        `para (b)` MEANS `ccc12 and` `the person steals, by s 2 steal` (JUST (`the person steals from any person` AND `at the time the person steals or immediately before or immediately thereafter, the person wounds, beats, strikes or uses any personal violence to that person`))
        `para (c)` MEANS JUST `the person assaults any person with intent to steal from them`
        `para (d)` MEANS `ccc12 and` `the person steals, by s 2 steal` (`ccc12 and` (JUST `the person steals from any person`) (`ccc12 or` `the person is armed with an offensive weapon, by s 2 offensive weapon` (JUST `the person is armed with an imitation of an offensive weapon`)))

§§ `Section 344 -- robbery: punishment, earlier offences`

`s 344(1)(a)(ii) seven years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 7, 0, 0, FALSE

-- (1)(a): a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used, or any firearm is used and the offence is for a criminal organization: life, with a minimum of five years (first offence) or seven years (second or subsequent). (b) any other case: life.
-- src:6756 | Robbery
-- src:6757 | 344 (1) Every person who commits robbery is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:6758 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:6759 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:6760 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:6761 | (a.1) [Repealed, 2022, c. 15, s. 12]
-- src:6762 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 344(1) (src:6756-6762)
GIVEN `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by s 344(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 344(1) the punishment for robbery` MEANS
    CONSIDER `limb (a) applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb with a minimum` (`imprisonment for life`)
                                    (IF `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by s 344(2)`
                                     THEN `imprisonment for a term of` `s 344(1)(a)(ii) seven years`   -- (a)(ii) second or subsequent offence
                                     ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`))   -- (a)(i) first offence
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for life`))   -- (b) in any other case
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an s 2.1, s 2 "firearm" or s 2 "criminal organization" answer was not given
    WHERE
        `limb (a) applies` MEANS
            `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm`)
                       (`ccc12 and` `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` (`ccc12 and` (JUST `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`) `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`))

-- src:6761 | (a.1) [Repealed, 2022, c. 15, s. 12]
@ref Criminal Code s 344(1)(a.1) (src:6761)
`s 344(1)(a.1) as the text shows it` MEANS "(a.1) [Repealed, 2022, c. 15, s. 12]"

-- "However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody."
-- "Ten years have elapsed" is read as: the day of the later conviction, less the days in custody, is on or after the tenth anniversary of the earlier conviction (fork F-DATE).
-- src:6768 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref Criminal Code s 344(2) ten years (src:6768)
GIVEN `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
      `the days of time in custody in between` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(2) ten years have elapsed between the convictions, not taking into account any time in custody` MEANS
    IF Day `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` MINUS `the days of time in custody in between`
           AT LEAST Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` PLUS 10))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- (2): the listed earlier offences are "considered as an earlier offence"; an earlier offence is not taken into account after 10 years.
-- (a) an offence under this section; (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- An offence outside the list is NOTHING (the list is not closed with "only").
-- src:6763 | Subsequent offences
-- src:6764 | (2) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (1)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:6765 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:6766 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:6767 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 344(2) (src:6763-6767)
GIVEN `the earlier offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ten years have elapsed, by s 344(2) ten years have elapsed between the convictions, not taking into account any time in custody` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(2) the earlier conviction is considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    IF `the earlier offence is on the list`
    THEN CONSIDER `ten years have elapsed, by s 344(2) ten years have elapsed between the convictions, not taking into account any time in custody`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of the ten-year period was not given
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence" does not say that any other offence is not
    WHERE
        `the earlier offence is on the list` MEANS `paragraph (a)` OR `paragraph (b)` OR `paragraph (c)`
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 344
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
                (`the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the earlier offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the earlier offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
             OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 244
             OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 244.2
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
                `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`
            AND (    `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 220
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 236
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 239
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 272
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 273
                  OR (`the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279 AND `the earlier offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279.1
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 346)

DECLARE `s 344(3) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 344(3) the sequence of convictions`
    `s 344(3) the sequence of commission of offences`
    `s 344(3) whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction`
    `s 344(3) any other matter`

-- src:6769 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:6770 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 344(3) (src:6769-6770)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 344(3) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(3) the matter is to be considered for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 344(3) the sequence of convictions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 344(3) the sequence of commission of offences` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences"
    WHEN `s 344(3) whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consideration shall be given to ... whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction"
    WHEN `s 344(3) any other matter` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"

§§ `Section 345 -- stopping mail`

-- src:6771 | Stopping mail with intent
-- src:6772 | 345 Every one who stops a mail conveyance with intent to rob or search it is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 345 (src:6771-6772)
GIVEN `the person stops a mail conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so with intent to rob or search it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 345 the person commits the offence of stopping mail with intent` MEANS
    IF `the person stops a mail conveyance` AND `the person does so with intent to rob or search it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who stops a mail conveyance with intent to rob or search it"

@ref Criminal Code s 345 (src:6772-6772)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 345 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for life`)

§§ `Section 346 -- extortion`

-- src:6773 | Extortion
-- src:6774 | 346 (1) Every one commits extortion who, without reasonable justification or excuse and with intent to obtain anything, by threats, accusations, menaces or violence induces or attempts to induce any person, whether or not he is the person threatened, accused or menaced or to whom violence is shown, to do anything or cause anything to be done.
@ref Criminal Code s 346(1) (src:6773-6774)
GIVEN `the person acted without reasonable justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted with intent to obtain anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted by threats, accusations, menaces or violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person induced or attempted to induce any person, whether or not that person is the person threatened, accused or menaced or to whom violence is shown, to do anything or cause anything to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(1) the person commits extortion` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without reasonable justification or excuse`
      AND `the person acted with intent to obtain anything`
      AND `the person acted by threats, accusations, menaces or violence`
      AND `the person induced or attempted to induce any person, whether or not that person is the person threatened, accused or menaced or to whom violence is shown, to do anything or cause anything to be done`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits extortion who, without reasonable justification or excuse and with intent to obtain anything, by threats, accusations, menaces or violence induces or attempts to induce any person"

`s 346(1.1)(a)(ii) seven years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 7, 0, 0, FALSE

-- src:6775 | Extortion
-- src:6776 | (1.1) Every person who commits extortion is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:6777 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:6778 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:6779 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:6780 | (a.1) [Repealed, 2022, c. 15, s. 13]
-- src:6781 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 346(1.1) (src:6775-6781)
GIVEN `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by s 346(1.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 346(1.1) the punishment for extortion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `limb (a) applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb with a minimum` (`imprisonment for life`)
                                    (IF `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by s 346(1.2)`
                                     THEN `imprisonment for a term of` `s 346(1.1)(a)(ii) seven years`   -- (a)(ii) second or subsequent offence
                                     ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`))   -- (a)(i) first offence
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for life`))   -- (b) in any other case
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an s 2.1, s 2 "firearm" or s 2 "criminal organization" answer was not given
    WHERE
        `limb (a) applies` MEANS
            `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm`)
                       (`ccc12 and` `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` (`ccc12 and` (JUST `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`) `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`))

-- src:6780 | (a.1) [Repealed, 2022, c. 15, s. 13]
@ref Criminal Code s 346(1.1)(a.1) (src:6780)
`s 346(1.1)(a.1) as the text shows it` MEANS "(a.1) [Repealed, 2022, c. 15, s. 13]"

-- (1.2): (a) an offence under this section; (b) 85(1) or (2) or 244 or 244.2; (c) 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, 279(1), 279.1 or 344 if a firearm was used. The same ten-year rule as 344(2) (the function of subsection 344(2) counts it).
-- src:6782 | Subsequent offences
-- src:6783 | (1.2) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (1.1)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:6784 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:6785 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:6786 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1 or 344 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:6787 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref Criminal Code s 346(1.2) (src:6782-6787)
GIVEN `the earlier offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ten years have elapsed, by s 344(2) ten years have elapsed between the convictions, not taking into account any time in custody` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(1.2) the earlier conviction is considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    IF `the earlier offence is on the list`
    THEN CONSIDER `ten years have elapsed, by s 344(2) ten years have elapsed between the convictions, not taking into account any time in custody`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of the ten-year period was not given
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection says which offences are considered, not that any other is not
    WHERE
        `the earlier offence is on the list` MEANS `paragraph (a)` OR `paragraph (b)` OR `paragraph (c)`
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 346
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
                (`the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the earlier offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the earlier offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
             OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 244
             OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 244.2
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
                `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`
            AND (    `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 220
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 236
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 239
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 272
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 273
                  OR (`the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279 AND `the earlier offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279.1
                  OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 344)

-- src:6788 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:6789 | (1.3) For the purposes of subsection (1.2), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 346(1.3) (src:6788-6789)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 344(3) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(1.3) the matter is to be considered for the purposes of subsection (1.2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 344(3) the sequence of convictions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 344(3) the sequence of commission of offences` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences"
    WHEN `s 344(3) whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consideration shall be given to ... whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction"
    WHEN `s 344(3) any other matter` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"

-- src:6790 | Aggravating factor
-- src:6791 | (1.4) If a person has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence must consider as an aggravating factor the fact that the offence was of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose.
@ref Criminal Code s 346(1.4) (src:6790-6791)
GIVEN `the person has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence under section 346` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(1.4) the court must consider as an aggravating factor that the offence was of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` MEANS
    IF `the person has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence under section 346` AND `the offence was of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person has been determined by a court to be guilty of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence must consider as an aggravating factor the fact that the offence was of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)

-- src:6792 | Saving
-- src:6793 | (2) A threat to institute civil proceedings is not a threat for the purposes of this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 346(2) (src:6792-6793)
GIVEN `the threat is a threat to institute civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(2) the threat is a threat for the purposes of section 346` MEANS
    IF `the threat is a threat to institute civil proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A threat to institute civil proceedings is not a threat for the purposes of this section"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says nothing of any other threat

-- src:6794 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:6795 | 346.1 A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under section 346 shall be served consecutively to any other sentence imposed on the person for an offence under any of sections 433 to 436 arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref Criminal Code s 346.1 (src:6794-6795)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under section 346` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the other offence arises out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346.1 the sentence shall be served consecutively to the other sentence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under section 346`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under section 346" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)
        IF `the other offence`'s `section` LESS THAN 433 OR `the other offence`'s `section` GREATER THAN 436
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of sections 433 to 436": an offence under another section is outside the list, which the text does not close with "only"
        IF NOT `the other offence arises out of the same event or series of events`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "arising out of the same event or series of events" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
